# Driver pedals, published by the pedal unit at the cycle rate of the VDC
# (docs/system_plan.md, sections 5.4 and 6.2). The pedal unit only measures; it
# sends no commands. The VDC maps the pedals to wheel torques; the drives use
# them directly in limp-home mode, the brake pedal before the drive pedal.
#
# Every pedal has two independent sensor channels. A channel value is the
# pedal travel from 0 (released) to 1 (fully pressed); NaN marks a failed
# channel.
#
# Payload 9 bytes, one CAN FD frame.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

float16[2] drive_pedal
# Drive (accelerator) pedal, channel 1 and 2.

float16[2] brake_pedal
# Brake pedal, channel 1 and 2.

bool drive_pedal_plausible
bool brake_pedal_plausible
# Both channels of the pedal agree within the tolerance of the pedal unit.
# A receiver uses an implausible drive pedal as released and an implausible
# brake pedal as the larger of its valid channels.

@extent 63 * 8
